  "answer": "General solution of g' + cos(g) = 0 from Wolfram Alpha: g(x) = 2 tan^(-1)(tanh(1/2 (c_1 - x))). Using the initial condition g(0) = 1, the integration constant is c_1 = 2 tanh^(-1)(tan(1/2)) (approximately 1.2262), so the solution is g(x) = 2 tan^(-1)(tanh(1/2 (2 tanh^(-1)(tan(1/2)) - x))). Wolfram Alpha's equivalent IVP form: g(x) = -sin^(-1)(coth(x - coth^(-1)(sin(1)))).",
